"id":"euler.lemma-2.1","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 2.1","locator":"Lemma 2.1, Section 2","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 2.1.** Let the wave vector $k(t)\\ne0$ and the amplitude vector $\\mathbf a(t)$, functions of time alone, satisfy $$\\begin{equation}\n k'=-D^Tk,\\qquad\n \\mathbf a'=-D\\mathbf a+p_{\\rm w} k,\\qquad\n p_{\\rm w}=\\frac{2k\\cdot D\\mathbf a}{|k|^2},\\qquad\n k\\cdot\\mathbf a=0. \\tag{2.1}\n\\end{equation}$$ Then $Dx+\\mathbf aF(k\\cdot x)$ is divergence free and solves the Euler equations on $\\mathbb R^3$ with pressure $-x\\cdot(D'+D^2)x/2-p_{\\rm w} P(k\\cdot x)$. If $k(t_0)\\ne0$, $\\mathbf a(t_0)\\ne0$ and $k(t_0)\\cdot\\mathbf a(t_0)=0$, then both vectors remain nonzero and perpendicular for every $t\\ge t_0$ in the interval of existence of $D$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-2.1","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-2.1","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.1%22%2C%22lean.TorusEuler.Paper.lemma_2_1%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.1%22%2C%22lean.TorusEuler.Paper.lemma_2_1%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/lean.TorusEuler.Paper.lemma_2_1"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-2.1","id":"field:0303bdc4ed0504de80203fc7f2c9fd1fb248e23c53d4393c1f48d8e5c782565a","kind":"citation_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-2.1","semantic_class":"provenance_field_refer